  "summary": "I worked all 8 items in your results inbox plus 5 that arrived while I was working. 12 are closed. One stays open on purpose: Leslie Parisian's chest X-ray (inbox-a0002) has only a preliminary read, and no final report has been issued, so RBC-INBOX-01 §2(c) says to leave it open. That preliminary read mentions a possible 7 mm right upper lobe nodule.\n\n**Two follow-ups for you:**\n1. **Old orders I couldn't cancel:** I have no tool to cancel a lab or imaging order. Two earlier orders now need to be discontinued by hand:\n   - **Walter Brennan's urgent repeat BMP (sr-t0016):** the stat BMP for today replaces it.\n   - **Raj Patel's 2027 lung screening CT (sr-t0001) and its tracking task (task-t0002):** the new 6-month CT replaces them. I made a task for you, due 10/26 (task-t0036).\n2. **Item in Dr. Reyes's queue (task-00002):** Mr. Patel has a potassium of 6.3 from 10/21 that nobody has acted on. The lab marked the sample hemolyzed. It isn't in your inbox, so I didn't act on it, but I sent Dr. Reyes an urgent message. Your messages queue (6 refill requests) was outside this request and I left it alone.\n\n**Raj Patel**\n- **CT urogram 10/19:** no kidney or bladder mass or stone. The 4 mm left lower lobe nodule it showed is already followed by his lung screening program. I first ordered his yearly screening CT for March–May 2027, with a tracking task, a message to him and a note.\n- **Screening addendum (arrived this morning):** Lakeshore Imaging's second reader found a new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule on his 4/14 scan and now recommends a CT at 6 months. That window runs to 11/14 and is still open. I ordered the CT for now through 11/14 (sr-t0034), with a tracking task due 11/14. I also sent him a corrected message and wrote an addendum note.\n\n**Edra Ondricka:** TSH was normal. Her potassium of 6.3 was corrected by the lab to 4.4 (analyzer fault). Both closed with no action.\n\n**Leslie Parisian**\n- **CT angiogram, preliminary read:** the final report replaces it. There is no clot and no nodule (the \"nodule\" was a blood vessel), and no follow-up imaging is needed. I closed it with that comment.\n- **BMP 10/22:** creatinine rose from 0.98 to 1.64 in 35 hours, which meets the kidney injury rule. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP for 10/23–10/26 and put his naproxen on hold. I messaged him today to stop ibuprofen and naproxen, and wrote a note.\n\n**Helen Marchetti**\n- **Creatinine 1.36 from 9/26:** this doesn't meet the kidney injury rule because there was no earlier value within 7 days. Closed with no action.\n- **New creatinine 1.48 on 10/22:** up from 0.88 on 10/21, which does meet the rule. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP for 10/23–10/26, held her naproxen, messaged her and wrote a note.\n\n**Carol Ann Whitfield**\n- **Creatinine 1.31 on 10/22:** doesn't meet the rule. I didn't use the 0.84 from 10/21 because it was entered in error. Closed with no action.\n- **New creatinine 1.78 that evening:** up 0.47 in 9 hours, which meets the rule. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP for 10/23–10/26, messaged her and wrote a note. Her hydrochlorothiazide, started 10/17 by Dr. Reyes, is noted for review; I didn't change it.\n\n**Walter Brennan**\n- **Potassium 6.4 on 10/22:** at first it was marked hemolyzed, so I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 and messaged him.\n- **Lab correction (this morning):** the hemolysis comment belonged to another patient's sample, so the 6.4 stands. I ordered a stat BMP for today (sr-t0020) and sent a stat message to the on-call pool. I also sent him a corrected message to come in today, with emergency warning signs, and wrote an addendum. His medications include nothing safe to hold for potassium.",
